[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-NAVIGATION-SUBMENU
TITLE: Navigation Submenu

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-447
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
A Navigation Submenu SHALL present the child Navigation Items of its parent entry, at most two submenu levels beneath a top-level entry, and SHALL omit deeper descendants from presentation.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Owner-locked depth keeps dropdowns and accordion expanders shallow while still exposing one nested child level under a first submenu.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-107
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-82
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-448
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
In wide chrome, a Navigation Submenu SHALL open as an overlay under its parent Navigation Item on hover or keyboard focus within that item, with the overlay's start edge aligned to the start edge of that parent item's label when that placement keeps the overlay inside the viewport, otherwise with the overlay's end edge aligned to the end edge of that parent item's label so the overlay stays inside the viewport; a nested Navigation Submenu in wide chrome SHALL open beside its parent Navigation Item toward the end when that placement keeps the overlay inside the viewport, otherwise toward the start so the overlay stays inside the viewport; and in mid and narrow chrome, a Navigation Submenu SHALL expand and collapse in place within the overlay Navigation Menu.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Wide chrome uses hover dropdown overlays whose preferred start edge tracks the parent label rather than the equal-grid cell edge, and flips to end-edge alignment or a startward nested flyout when needed so trailing items stay on-screen. Mid and narrow chrome use accordion expansion inside the menu overlay.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-107
GSSC5-137
GSSC5-143
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-83
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-84
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-449
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
A Navigation Submenu overlay in wide chrome SHALL use the white theme token for its background, the gray theme token for its border, and the dark-green theme token for its text.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Dropdown surfaces match other Header overlay panels so nested destinations stay readable over page content.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-107
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-84
  ROLE: Refines

