- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-109
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-666
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
In wide chrome, the Nested Submenu Pointer Bridge SHALL occupy the triangular region from the current pointer position to the near vertical edge of the open nested Navigation Submenu, and SHALL leave the residual area beside that triangle free for sibling Navigation Item hits.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A triangle from the pointer to the nested submenu near edge covers the diagonal path; residual space must not block vertical sibling selection.
<<<
