[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-ANNOUNCEMENT-EDITOR-BEHAVIORS
TITLE: Announcement Editor Behaviors

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-300
TITLE: Catalog Load
STATEMENT: >>>
When the Announcements Editor Page opens for a signed-in member, the Announcement Catalog SHALL load announcement headers from the Unified Backend announcements list for that member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authenticated list retrieval is the GSSC5-68 member announcement list contract.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-45
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-301
TITLE: Create Announcement
STATEMENT: >>>
When Save succeeds on the Announcement Editor in create mode with a selected Content Template and non-empty Body, the Member Frontend SHALL create the announcement through the Unified Backend announcements create contract and then show that announcement in the Catalog for further modification.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Creation without developer intervention uses the existing announcements POST API and template identity required by that API.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-43
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-302
TITLE: Modify Announcement
STATEMENT: >>>
When Save succeeds on the Announcement Editor for an existing announcement, the Member Frontend SHALL write the Header and Body through the Unified Backend announcements modify contract for that announcement.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authorized members correct announcements after create without developer intervention.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-45
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-303
TITLE: Publish Announcement
STATEMENT: >>>
When the member sets Publication Target on the Announcement Editor and Save persists that choice, the Member Frontend SHALL publish the announcement so Member Frontend only maps to not public, and Public Frontend or both map to public, using the Unified Backend announcements modify visibility contract.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
MHLR publication targets Public, Member, or both; the GSSC5-68 wire visibility flag is isPublic, which distinguishes members-only from public (also visible to members).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-44
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-304
TITLE: Cancel Discard
STATEMENT: >>>
When Cancel is activated on the Announcement Editor, the Member Frontend SHALL restore Header, Body, Publication Target, and Content Template fields to the last loaded or last saved baseline without writing to the Unified Backend.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Cancel must discard unsaved announcement edits.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-45
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-305
TITLE: Template Required For Create
STATEMENT: >>>
While the Announcement Editor is in create mode, the Member Frontend SHALL require a Content Template selection before Save can create the announcement, and SHALL load available templates from the Unified Backend templates list for the signed-in member.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Announcement create on the Unified Backend requires a template identity.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-43
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-306
TITLE: Editor Mode Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
Selecting an announcement in the Catalog SHALL load that announcement into the Announcement Editor for modification, and activating create SHALL clear the editor into create mode with a distinct exclusive-edit resource identity until creation succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Create and modify are different editor modes sharing one Generic Editor host; exclusive edit keys must not collide across drafts and stored announcements.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-94
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-43
  ROLE: Refines
