[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-DASHBOARD-MODIFICATION
TITLE: Dashboard Section Modification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-MLLR-237
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When the logged-in member has the necessary permissions, the Dashboard Page SHALL host a Generic Editor for each dashboard section so that member can change that section's header, body, and image position without programming knowledge; Save SHALL persist those values to the Unified Backend for that section; Cancel SHALL discard unsaved changes for that section; and after a successful Save the page SHALL refresh that section's displayed Contents.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authorized members keep dashboard wording current through the shared Generic Editor Module. Persistence stays with the Unified Backend section update. Refreshing display after Save keeps the read-only section view aligned with saved Contents.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
GSSC5-89. Necessary permissions are those the Unified Backend accepts for section modification. The Member Frontend omits editors when the member lacks that authority. Wave 7 content editors remain the broader authoring surfaces for other page kinds.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-89
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-MHLR-28
  ROLE: Refines

