The Site Tree Editor Page SHALL place its heading, frontend selector, tree outline, and node editor panel in the Page Outlet at full content width, with the tree outline beside or above the node editor panel so both remain visible together on a wide viewport, and SHALL keep the tree outline region and the node editor panel independently scrollable when either region's contents grow taller than the available layout height.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Administrators need the outline and the selected-node fields in one composition without leaving the page. Independent pane scroll keeps selection and editing usable when either side grows long.
